used only during peak hours."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d01", "start": 364, "end": 404, "text": "Araki Station opened on January 1, 1960."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d01", "start": 405, "end": 470, "text": "A footbridge and the north entrance were opened on April 1, 1979."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d01", "start": 471, "end": 597, "text": "The station was absorbed into the JR East network upon the privatization of Japanese National Railways (JNR) on April 1, 1987."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d02", "start": 0, "end": 40, "text": "ticket window and a narrow waiting area."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d02", "start": 41, "end": 100, "text": "Access to the island platforms is by means of a footbridge."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d02", "start": 101, "end": 257, "text": "Management of the station has been outsourced to the JR Kyushu Tetsudou Eigyou Co., a wholly owned subsidiary of JR Kyushu specialising in station services."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d02", "start": 258, "end": 343, "text": "It staffs the ticket counter which is equipped with a \"Midori no Madoguchi\" facility."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d02", "start": 344, "end": 489, "text": "The station was opened by Japanese Government Railways (JGR) on 20 April 1910 as an additional station on the existing Kagoshima Main Line track."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d02", "start": 490, "end": 603, "text": "With the privatization of Japanese National Railways (JNR), the successor of JGR, on 1 April 1987, JR Kyushu took"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0297-66fe6aebaf4b:d03", "start": 0, "end": 609, "text": "Wikipedia image V